      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>spec.tlsSecurityProfile.type</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the TLS security profile type (<code>Old</code>, <code>Intermediate</code>, or <code>Custom</code>). The default is <code>Intermediate</code>.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>spec.tlsSecurityProfile.type.custom</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the appropriate field for the selected type: *   <code>old: {"{"}{"}"}</code> *   <code>intermediate: {"{"}{"}"}</code> *   <code>modern: {"{"}{"}"}</code> *   <code>custom:</code></p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>spec.tlsSecurityProfile.type.custom</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>For the <code>custom</code> type, specifies a list of TLS ciphers and the minimum accepted TLS version.</p></dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>spec.machineConfigPoolSelector.matchLabels.custom</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the machine config pool label for the nodes you want to apply the TLS security profile. This parameter is optional.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the <code>KubeletConfig</code> object:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create -f <filename>"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>Depending on the number of worker nodes in the cluster, wait for the configured nodes to be rebooted one by one.</p>
